WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.269 --> 00:00:09.049
The edgy kids who make up the DC Extended
Universe's Suicide Squad are a far cry from

00:00:09.049 --> 00:00:12.340
the comics' original team of straightlaced
heroes.

00:00:12.340 --> 00:00:16.790
While the original crew simply strove for
the benefit of mankind, the modern Squad's

00:00:16.790 --> 00:00:19.860
interests are generally a bit more unpredictable.

00:00:19.860 --> 00:00:23.840
Which is not to say that the Suicide Squad
hasn't always been filled with a fair dose

00:00:23.840 --> 00:00:25.340
of crazy.

00:00:25.340 --> 00:00:28.720
Here's a look at the Squad's weird history.

00:00:28.720 --> 00:00:30.130
Origins

00:00:30.130 --> 00:00:35.800
Secret Origins #14 reveals that Squadron S
was where the Army put all of their crazier

00:00:35.800 --> 00:00:39.230
soldiers, who would either get the job done...
or kill each other.

00:00:39.230 --> 00:00:43.640
The crew took the name "Suicide Squad" not
because they were willing to die, but because

00:00:43.640 --> 00:00:49.030
most soldiers would rather kill themselves
than join Squadron S. The dysfunctional team

00:00:49.030 --> 00:00:53.500
is headed up by Rick Flag Sr., and they’re
called into action to fight super-threats

00:00:53.500 --> 00:00:57.469
after the Justice Society of America temporarily
quits.

00:00:57.469 --> 00:01:02.829
Much later, Rick Flag Jr. takes over his dad’s
legacy after Rick Sr. kills himself fighting

00:01:02.829 --> 00:01:06.500
the War Wheel, while still in mourning for
his deceased wife.

00:01:06.500 --> 00:01:11.990
Flag Jr.’s team first appears in 1959’s
The Brave and the Bold #25.

00:01:11.990 --> 00:01:17.549
Colonel Rick Flag Jr., Karin Grace, Jess Bright,
and Dr. Hugh Evans are all the last living

00:01:17.549 --> 00:01:21.959
members of their respective teams, all willing
to die to save the world and uplift their

00:01:21.959 --> 00:01:23.679
lost friends' legacies.

00:01:23.679 --> 00:01:27.450
They're basically a crew powered by pure survivor's
guilt.

00:01:27.450 --> 00:01:31.609
Even in their first appearance fighting a
giant, red-hot dinosaur, the Squad makes it

00:01:31.609 --> 00:01:36.229
clear that they're a bit suicidal—but for
all the right reasons.

00:01:36.229 --> 00:01:40.570
After about fifty issues, Bright and Evans
are swallowed up in an icy crevasse while

00:01:40.570 --> 00:01:42.029
battling a yeti.

00:01:42.029 --> 00:01:45.560
The team disbands, and the two are assumed
dead for years.

00:01:45.560 --> 00:01:49.939
Bright, however, survives by pulling a page
right out of Star Wars and digging himself

00:01:49.939 --> 00:01:52.210
into the warm yeti carcass.

00:01:52.210 --> 00:01:56.689
The Chinese government eventually finds him,
removes his busted body parts, and uses their

00:01:56.689 --> 00:02:01.239
own super soldier program to rescue him so
they can use his scientific genius.

00:02:01.239 --> 00:02:06.639
Bright, now angry and insane, goes on to create
a terrorist supervillain team called The Jihad,

00:02:06.639 --> 00:02:09.220
who plague the Squad for decades.

00:02:09.220 --> 00:02:13.430
After the team disbands and re-forms, the
Suicide Squad again becomes the repository

00:02:13.430 --> 00:02:14.670
for the unwanted.

00:02:14.670 --> 00:02:19.990
But instead of just really bad soldiers, Flag
Jr. has to manage semi-reformed supervillains.

00:02:19.990 --> 00:02:25.250
The Squad is a great place for DC Comics to
put their stranger villains, digging up obscure

00:02:25.250 --> 00:02:27.920
comic history along the way.

00:02:27.920 --> 00:02:28.920
Harley Quinn

00:02:28.920 --> 00:02:34.920
Dr. Harleen Quinzel entered DC Comics as an
underqualified Arkham Asylum psychiatrist

00:02:34.920 --> 00:02:37.970
who falls under the Joker's gross spell.

00:02:37.970 --> 00:02:42.500
She became a fan favorite villain pretty quickly,
but most readers seem to just ignore the fact

00:02:42.500 --> 00:02:46.450
that the Joker has tried to kill Harley more
times than her enemies ever have.

00:02:46.450 --> 00:02:51.100
Despite regular abuse, her infatuation with
the Clown Prince of Crime continued for about

00:02:51.100 --> 00:02:56.450
two decades…until her writers realized that
depicting an abusive relationship as endearing

00:02:56.450 --> 00:02:58.040
wasn't really responsible.

00:02:58.040 --> 00:03:03.410
In Harley Quinn #25, she beat the Joker to
a pulp in his own prison cell, completely

00:03:03.410 --> 00:03:08.380
biting off his lower lip in the process, making
it very hard for him to smile that winning

00:03:08.380 --> 00:03:09.380
grin.

00:03:09.380 --> 00:03:10.380
Deadshot

00:03:10.380 --> 00:03:15.950
Floyd Lawton is an assassin with a heart of
gold and a cyborg eye who embodies the spirit

00:03:15.950 --> 00:03:18.770
of the Suicide Squad better than any other
member.

00:03:18.770 --> 00:03:23.290
He has no wish to live, refuses to commit
suicide, and wants to die in an honorable

00:03:23.290 --> 00:03:24.490
way.

00:03:24.490 --> 00:03:28.819
Deadshot's strangest adventure is set off
by an airport employee who steals his costume

00:03:28.819 --> 00:03:33.850
from his luggage and goes around killing innocent
people, forcing the real Deadshot to, well,

00:03:33.850 --> 00:03:35.370
shoot him dead.

00:03:35.370 --> 00:03:39.650
Shooting a guy dressed as himself messes up
Deadshot for a while… until he's possessed

00:03:39.650 --> 00:03:43.930
by a demon, tries to blow up some kids in
an elementary school, and then tries to kill

00:03:43.930 --> 00:03:44.930
the Pope.

00:03:44.930 --> 00:03:49.730
Which is probably the worst thing a comic
character has ever attempted.

00:03:49.730 --> 00:03:51.210
El Diablo

00:03:51.210 --> 00:03:56.200
The name El Diablo has generally applied to
heroic characters in DC's history, but the

00:03:56.200 --> 00:04:01.100
modern El Diablo is first seen accidentally
killing the entire innocent family of a rival

00:04:01.100 --> 00:04:02.150
gang member.

00:04:02.150 --> 00:04:06.900
He seeks redemption by joining the Squad and
frequently voices his objections to any senseless

00:04:06.900 --> 00:04:07.959
killing.

00:04:07.959 --> 00:04:11.850
During his very first outing with the Squad,
the team has to contain a stadium full of

00:04:11.850 --> 00:04:16.019
humans infected with a robo-virus that kinda
turns them into zombies.

00:04:16.019 --> 00:04:20.579
When El Diablo and Deadshot are attacked by
a pregnant woman-bot, Diablo is the one who

00:04:20.579 --> 00:04:22.949
protects her from being killed.

00:04:22.949 --> 00:04:27.810
She mutates into a crazy Jabba blob, King
Shark bites her head off, and the team delivers

00:04:27.810 --> 00:04:31.050
a healthy baby by slicing it out of the monster's
belly.

00:04:31.050 --> 00:04:35.599
The whole thing sets off a rivalry between
Diablo and Deadshot.

00:04:35.599 --> 00:04:36.909
Katana

00:04:36.909 --> 00:04:41.259
While most of these Suicide Squad members
are part of Batman's rogues' gallery, Katana

00:04:41.259 --> 00:04:44.710
actually worked alongside Batman in his team,
the Outsiders.

00:04:44.710 --> 00:04:49.580
She still doesn't completely fit into the
"superhero" model, as she wields a sword that

00:04:49.580 --> 00:04:54.580
steals souls, and heroes generally like to
leave souls in the bodies they came from.

00:04:54.580 --> 00:04:58.620
Katana's sword has a pretty special relationship
with death, so the heroine was able to help

00:04:58.620 --> 00:05:03.759
stop the Black Lantern zombies' plans when
they invaded Earth during the epic DC Comics

00:05:03.759 --> 00:05:05.080
event, Blackest Night.

00:05:05.080 --> 00:05:10.229
So while carrying around a sword full of tortured
souls is a pretty sucky superpower to have,

00:05:10.229 --> 00:05:12.210
it's not altogether useless.

00:05:12.210 --> 00:05:16.690
Corpse whispering is a pretty profitable backup
plan if the whole hero thing doesn't work

00:05:16.690 --> 00:05:17.690
out.

00:05:17.690 --> 00:05:19.070
Just ask John Edward.

00:05:19.070 --> 00:05:20.070
Enchantress

00:05:20.070 --> 00:05:24.889
If you go to a party at a creepy castle, don't
wander around, or else you run the risk of

00:05:24.889 --> 00:05:27.460
being possessed by an ancient space witch.

00:05:27.460 --> 00:05:29.009
That's just common sense.

00:05:29.009 --> 00:05:31.909
Unfortunately, June Moone didn't get the memo.

00:05:31.909 --> 00:05:36.439
Now she plays host to a powerful evil that
she can only sometimes control, causing her

00:05:36.439 --> 00:05:39.909
to unpredictably slip between hero and villain.

00:05:39.909 --> 00:05:44.500
After a while, the forces that gave Enchantress
her powers went rotten, so she turned crazy

00:05:44.500 --> 00:05:48.120
and attacked Supergirl, earning her new villain
status.

00:05:48.120 --> 00:05:53.479
Enchantress has been separated from and reunited
with the dark soul that fuels her a few times,

00:05:53.479 --> 00:05:58.830
leaving her catatonic or tucked safely away
in an asylum, so she's kinda damned either

00:05:58.830 --> 00:05:59.830
way.

00:05:59.830 --> 00:06:04.099
All of this makes her a pretty good candidate
for the Suicide Squad.

00:06:04.099 --> 00:06:05.669
Captain Boomerang

00:06:05.669 --> 00:06:09.599
Remember the time you brought your teddy bear
to school and everyone laughed at you, so

00:06:09.599 --> 00:06:13.430
you decided to go home and become a teddy
bear-themed supervillain?

00:06:13.430 --> 00:06:17.699
That's pretty much the origin story of Captain
Boomerang, except with boomerangs.

00:06:17.699 --> 00:06:22.409
Digger Harkness is probably one of the worst
humans alive in the DC Universe.

00:06:22.409 --> 00:06:26.770
He's outwardly racist, he's cowardly, and
he went on a pie-throwing rampage against

00:06:26.770 --> 00:06:29.830
his teammates that lasted a year and a half.

00:06:29.830 --> 00:06:33.689
Eventually, everyone got so tired of him that
he was dropped on a deserted island until

00:06:33.689 --> 00:06:35.419
the Squad needed him again.

00:06:35.419 --> 00:06:39.379
When he was picked up, he'd grown a wicked
beard and was trying to build a giant boomerang

00:06:39.379 --> 00:06:44.139
to fly himself home—because not only is
he a jerk, but he's pretty stupid too.

00:06:44.139 --> 00:06:45.879
His first mission back?

00:06:45.879 --> 00:06:50.190
Dressing up like Batman to distract some bad
guys, because Captain Boomerang’ best power

00:06:50.190 --> 00:06:52.979
is being a human target.

00:06:52.979 --> 00:06:54.460
Killer Croc

00:06:54.460 --> 00:06:59.569
Waylon Jones has more origin stories than
teeth, and that's a lot for a man-eating crocodile

00:06:59.569 --> 00:07:00.759
person.

00:07:00.759 --> 00:07:05.629
Whether his condition was caused by a skin
disease, a gypsy curse, bad steroids, or genetic

00:07:05.629 --> 00:07:11.199
experiments gone wrong, Croc is now a guy
who is super strong, super dumb, and hungry

00:07:11.199 --> 00:07:12.379
for living meat.

00:07:12.379 --> 00:07:16.959
"When Batman came nosing around, he was getting
closer...closer."

00:07:17.100 --> 00:07:18.100
"And?"

00:07:18.100 --> 00:07:21.000
"I threw a rock at him!"

00:07:21.009 --> 00:07:25.699
Croc actually has a special relationship with
DC weirdo Swamp Thing.

00:07:25.699 --> 00:07:30.039
At one point, Swamp Thing lures Croc into
breaking out of Arkham, causing Batman to

00:07:30.039 --> 00:07:32.919
pursue him all the way to Louisiana.

00:07:32.919 --> 00:07:37.089
After a battle through the muck, Swamp Thing
subdues Batman with a puff of psychotropic

00:07:37.089 --> 00:07:42.589
pollen, convincing Batman to let the animalistic
Croc finally find peace and solitude in the

00:07:42.589 --> 00:07:46.219
swamps… at least for a little while.

00:07:46.219 --> 00:07:47.219
Slipknot

00:07:47.219 --> 00:07:51.330
Years before the metal band of the same name
made its debut, Slipknot was a forgettable

00:07:51.330 --> 00:07:52.330
villain.

00:07:52.330 --> 00:07:57.360
The bad guy is first seen attacking DC hero
Firestorm, using a gimmick even worse than

00:07:57.360 --> 00:07:59.979
Captain Boomerang's boomerangs: ropes.

00:07:59.979 --> 00:08:03.180
Sure, they're durable ropes, but they're still
ropes.

00:08:03.180 --> 00:08:07.729
And even though DC Comics already had its
ultimate durable rope in Wonder Woman's Lasso

00:08:07.729 --> 00:08:10.800
of Truth, they still needed more ropes.

00:08:10.800 --> 00:08:13.050
And that's Slipknot.

00:08:13.050 --> 00:08:15.669
Slipknot's worst moment comes at the hands
of Boomerang.

00:08:15.669 --> 00:08:20.149
In order to keep the Suicide Squad in check,
each member is fitted with explosive wristbands

00:08:20.149 --> 00:08:23.939
that can't go beyond a certain range or they'll
explode.

00:08:23.939 --> 00:08:28.499
Boomerang isn't keen on using himself to test
whether or not these explosive devices are

00:08:28.499 --> 00:08:31.869
real, so he convinces Slipknot that they’re
fake.

00:08:31.869 --> 00:08:38.080
Slipknot takes the first opportunity to escape…only
to have his arm blown off by a very real explosive

00:08:38.080 --> 00:08:39.080
wrist bomb.

00:08:39.080 --> 00:08:41.720
Which makes it pretty hard to tie slipknots
for a while.

00:08:41.720 --> 00:08:43.380
Thanks for watching!

00:08:43.380 --> 00:08:47.100
Subscribe to our YouTube channel to watch
more videos like the one you just saw.

00:08:47.100 --> 00:08:50.940
And leave us a comment to let us know your
favorite Suicide Squad member...

